{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788220924,"nonce":"CBEV3cLK66dekffM1ObrFVr+uY4=","message":"Legibility fixture STAGED ON PAPER and merged (4b60f3f). The blocker was never\nthe render — it was that autostart.rws has no enclosed rooms and no stove, so\nquestions 1 and 3 had no correct answer to grade against.\n\nTwo findings worth carrying beyond this issue:\n\n**No roof is needed, and it is a good thing, because nothing in the verb surface\ncan place one.** `area build-roof add` only DESIGNATES and then waits for a\ncolonist. But `Room.PsychologicallyOutdoors` needs 300 open-roof cells (or a\nmap-edge room half unroofed) and `ProperRoom` is `!TouchesMapEdge` plus a Normal\ndistrict — so an unroofed 11x7 away from the map edge is already two proper\nindoor rooms, and `UpdateRoomStatsAndRole` scores the stove room 28 as a\n`RoomRoleWorker_Kitchen`. A fixture that required roofing could not have been\nstaged with the verbs that exist.\n\n**--landmarks WAS NEVER PASSING, and the earlier reading of it was wrong.**\nSession 9 recorded that renders with and without the flag produced an identical\nhash. That was an EMPTY REGISTRY, not agreement: `landmark --list` returned {},\nso there was nothing to draw. The path is untested, not proven. The plain\n`landmark {set:{name,at}}` verb writes the registry and is NOT dev-gated, so it\ncan be exercised — and the check is now INVERTED: two landmarks inside the rect,\nand the two renders MUST DIFFER. The landmark render is taken after the graded\nones so a landmark never labels an answer on an image a reader has to judge.\n\nFiled out of this work: `2a7c064` (p3) — `_label_pass` adds `size/2` to a\nposition that is already the centre, so an odd-width building's code draws one\ncell east of true centre. It sits on this issue's own acceptance path, because\nquestion 4 grades stove cells against the published centre.\n\nStill owed here: the fixture has NOT been run, and the legibility read needs a\nFRESH READER PER ITERATION — a reader that has seen one render cannot judge the\nnext. Both are the orchestrator's to do.","files":null}]}